{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Tips on IT Procurement: Suppliers Must Not Walk away"}, {"type": "position", "content": 10}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about suppliers and timeframes."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about people's backgrounds in spoken or written documents.  Participate in the improvement of IT contracts, establishing technical clauses that respond to the needs of the negotiating agents, based on current laws on contracting."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of a range of grammar and vocabulary, and with the appropriate level of formality and purpose, coherence and cohesion for the context.  Recognizes simple ideas on concepts on IT contracts and knowledge transfer, simulated processes of IT contracting, and technological negociation."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "comply"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to act in correspondence with something stipulated in a contract or law"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's been hard to make him comply with some things. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob10aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "docket "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "schedule; agenda "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As it happens a lot, the best thing you can do is to have a docket devoted to the tasks that may be performed by either you or the supplier."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob10aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "liquidated damages "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "amount of money (agreed through a contract) any party obtains in case of aggravation "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Well, liquidated damages can be payables if milestones are not met."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob10aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "payable"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a debt owed to a creditor"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Well, liquidated damages can be payables if milestones are not met."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob10aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "performance warranty "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an agreement between two parties for one of them to perform all of its obligations under the contract "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A performance warranty must be included. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob10aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "timeframe "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an interval of time within something planned or expected to happen "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The excuse that can be given by them is that timeframes are dependent on the customer doing their part, which results in the supplier trying to find an \u2018out' for delays caused by the customer.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob10aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about consequences of not complying in a project you are interested in."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Describe how strong each of the possible consequences is."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 2 paragraphs about those consequences. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read them to a classmate."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I can look for specific information on the internet."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can describe the different consequences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can write paragraphs about the consequences of not complying."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Passive Questions with Modal verbs "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Use questions in the <span class =\"strong\"> passive voice </span> using <span class =\"strong\"> modal verbs </span> to request  information about what the object can do in terms of possibility, advisability, and necessity, among others."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The main difference between a regular question with a modal verb and one using the <span class =\"strong\"> passive voice </span>, however, is that the modal verb in the latter goes between the subject and the verb to be. That is because when using passive voice, you don't mind about the doer but the action itself. <br/><br/> Let's remember the structure you use to make a question using the <span class =\"strong\"> passive voice </span> of <span class =\"strong\"> modal verbs </span>. <br/><br/> <div class=\"center_text\"> <span class =\"strong\">(WH) + Modal + Subject + be + verb (past participle) + complement + ?</span> </div>  <br/><br/> Examples: <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class =\"strong\"> What can be done </span> to prevent supplier to walk away from their responsibilities? <br/> <span class =\"strong\"> Should the supplier be held </span> accountable for all the contractual responsibilities? </span> <br/><br/> Remember, that the passive voice is used in formal contexts, and it is used to give a special importance on the object of the sentence."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Can suppliers be held accountable for timeframes?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "What else should be done?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Should refunds be made if the solution does not work as planned?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modal verbs in Passive Voice to Answer Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The <span class =\"strong\"> passive voice </span> is normally used when we don't know who the agent of an action is or it is not important; therefore, all the importance is given to the object of the sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use the modals <span class =\"strong\"> can be </span> or <span class =\"strong\"> could be + past participle </span> to talk about present and past ability or possibility in the <span class =\"strong\"> passive voice </span>: <br/><br/> <li><span class=\"italic\"> A timeframe <span class =\"strong\"> can be negotiated </span> with the supplier.</span></li> <br/> We use <span class =\"strong\"> must be / have to be / ought to be / should be + past participle </span> forms to talk about necessity and advisability in the passive voice: <br/><br/> <li><span class=\"italic\"> Something <span class =\"strong\"> must be done </span> to make that supplier comply with the timeframe.</span></li> <br/> The following chart explains in detail the structure one should follow to make a sentence using the passive voice:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":5,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Object\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main verb  (past participle)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Complement (Agent)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"timeframes\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Should\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"respected\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"by all the parties in a contract.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n7le03ob10re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n7le03ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<p><strong>Lucy: </strong>So, tell me, Tom. How&rsquo;s everything going with your new business?&nbsp;<br /><strong>Tom:</strong> Not as good as planned, I&rsquo;m afraid I&rsquo;ve been having real issues with my software supplier.<br /><strong>Lucy: </strong>How come?<br /><strong>Tom:</strong> It&rsquo;s been hard to make him comply with some things. Can suppliers be held accountable for timeframes?</p>"}, {"time": "21000", "image": "enpe8n7le03ob10re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<p><strong>Lucy:</strong> Of course. A defined project plan with key milestones has to be included for the supplier to meet. It is really important to clarify the consequences that may be in case the supplier doesn&rsquo;t comply with their part on time. The excuse that can be given by them is that timeframes are dependent on the customer doing their part, which results in the supplier trying to find an &lsquo;out&rsquo; for delays caused by the customer. As it happens a lot, the best thing you can do is to have a docket devoted to the tasks that may be performed by either you or the supplier.<br /><strong>Tom:</strong> Interesting. Yet I have done everything from my part. What else should be done?</p>"}, {"time": "65000", "image": "enpe8n7le03ob10re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<p><strong>Lucy:</strong> A performance warranty must be included. The supplier should understand his obligations, so he doesn&rsquo;t just walk away from the project. This warranty offers a practical remedy in circumstances where a remedy may be otherwise unavailable. You can also obtain a right to perform acceptance testing. Whether they like it or not, suppliers must agree to these terms.<br /><strong>Tom:</strong> Are there any consequences for the supplier if he doesn&rsquo;t comply with any of these?<br /><strong>Lucy:</strong> Well, liquidated damages can be payables if milestones are not met; likewise, the supplier can also be sued for damages.<br /><strong>Tom:</strong> Should refunds be made if the solution does not work as planned?<br /><strong>Lucy:</strong> Sure, you can always obtain a refund of the fees paid.</p>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n7le03ob10re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the importance of holding suppliers to a timeframe. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can discuss performance warranties to prevent suppliers from walking away. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about possible consequences for suppliers when not fulfilling the established requirements."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "When signing a software license, how do you make sure the suppliers are going to deliver their part on time? Explain."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What kind of consequences should be necessary for a supplier to be attached to the timeframes proposed in a contract?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {